     l10n_din5008's footer renders company.company_registry unconditionally
     (empty <li> still takes up space in the list). For Swiss companies the
     UID doubles as the commercial registry number since the 2011 reform, so
     company_registry is often set to the exact same value as vat - showing
     both lines then just duplicates the same number under two labels, so
     also hide it when it matches vat. Not brand-specific, just a general
     cleanup for this company's chosen layout. -->
<odoo>
    <template id="external_layout_din5008_hide_empty_registry" inherit_id="l10n_din5008.external_layout_din5008">
        <xpath expr="//li[span[@t-field='company.company_registry']]" position="attributes">
            <attribute name="t-if">company.company_registry and company.company_registry != company.vat</attribute>
        </xpath>
    </template>
</odoo>
